Exactly those with $5 \mid m_1 + \cdots + m_5$ and, writing $s = m_1 + m_2 + m_4 + m_5$:
if $m_2 - m_1 \le m_5 - m_4$, one of (i) $m_5 - m_4 \ge 2m_3 - m_1 - m_2$; (ii) $s$ even and $\min\!\left(m_4 - m_3,\ m_3 - \frac{m_1 + m_2 + m_5 - m_4}{2}\right)$ even; (iii) $s$ odd and $m_4 + m_5 - 2m_3 > 2m_3 - m_1 - m_2$;
if $m_2 - m_1 > m_5 - m_4$, one of (i) $m_2 - m_1 \ge m_4 + m_5 - 2m_3$; (ii) $s$ even and $\min\!\left(m_3 - m_2,\ \frac{m_1 - m_2 + m_4 + m_5}{2} - m_3\right)$ even; (iii) $s$ odd and $2m_3 - m_1 - m_2 > m_4 + m_5 - 2m_3$.
